  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader who picks an accent hue, I want links and the accent to stay readable on the standard dark page, so that a red or blue accent is not hard to read now that the page is legacy's grey (#2E2F33) and no longer black. (Found by the adversarial review of #1212, the fix of #1210.)\n\n### Observed\n\n- Contrast of the night accent (and links) on the reader page, recomputed in the review of #1212: on the #2E2F33 page, **161 of the 360 slider hues fall under 4.5:1** (hues 0–12° and 212–359°); on the old black page 37 did.\n- Examples: hue 0° (red) 3.71:1 (5.82:1 on black); hue 220° 3.64:1 (5.72:1 on black).\n- `ThemeAppearanceTests` checks the accent for the default hue (190°) only.\n- Legacy uses the same grey and the same accent formula, so this matches legacy; it is a readability gap that #1210's move to the grey made wider.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Sweep every hue (0–359°) against `ThemeAppearance.readerSurfaces` for the standard dark style, with the contrast helper of `ThemeAppearanceTests`.\n- Decide, with the operator, whether to lift the night accent's brightness in standard dark above legacy's formula (a deliberate difference to record), or to accept legacy's values and say so.\n- LOT-180 (single accent) owns the accent's contrast; coordinate.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A test that sweeps the hues and pins the decision (a lower bound, or the list of exceptions).\n\n### Sources\n\n- #1210, #1212 (review round 3), `docs/lots/LOT-122-appearance.md` (Contrast).",
